          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: The GEIPAN received numerous witness reports of a bright phenomenon passing through the sky on January 24, 2012, around 7:50 a.m., over the Lorraine region. All of these witness reports clearly correspond to the observation of a meteor: the entry into the Earth's atmosphere of a naturally occurring meteoroid (small asteroid). The reform-meteor network also identifies this event as a naturally occurring meteor. This case is classified \"A.\"",
